---
const constraints = [
  {
    index: "01",
    title: "Sustained Event Throughput",
    detail:
      "Detector readouts and front-end links produce tens to hundreds of millions of frames per second. Mutex-protected queues collapse under cache-line ping-ponging.",
  },
  {
    index: "02",
    title: "Bounded Tail Latency",
    detail:
      "Online triggers operate under hard read-out buffers. An unpredictable p99.9 latency spike overflows front-end FIFOs and loses physics events.",
  },
  {
    index: "03",
    title: "Zero-Allocation Hot Paths",
    detail:
      "Dynamic heap allocations, virtual dispatch, and ad-hoc locks on the ingest thread inject jitter and stall instruction pipelines at microsecond scales.",
  },
  {
    index: "04",
    title: "Verifiable Integrity",
    detail:
      "Persisted pages require hardware-speed checksums, deterministic offline replay, and formal proofs guarantees that lock-free protocols never tear or deadlock.",
  },
];
---

<section id="problem" class="border-b border-white/[0.06] bg-[#131316] py-24 sm:py-32">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 sm:px-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-14 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
      <!-- Editorial left column -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.14em] text-[#3B82F6] uppercase">
          The Problem
        </p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-[#F4F5F7] sm:text-4xl sm:leading-[1.15]">
          High-rate telemetry breaks general-purpose queues.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-[#A1A6B3] sm:text-[17px]">
          In high-energy physics data acquisition and cryogenic sensor readouts, data movement cannot borrow time from locks, page faults, or heap allocators.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[#6E7485]">
          ChronoRing mirrors proven online-DAQ patterns: cache-line-aligned ring buffering, Structure-of-Arrays vector filtering, and direct memory-mapped persistence with formal safety models.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Constraint grid right column -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:col-span-7">
        {constraints.map((c) => (
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/[0.08] bg-[#202126]/65 p-7 transition-colors duration-200 hover:border-white/[0.15] hover:bg-[#202126]">
            <div class="font-mono text-xs font-medium text-[#3B82F6]">{c.index}</div>
            <h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.015em] text-[#F4F5F7]">
              {c.title}
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[#A1A6B3]">
              {c.detail}
            </p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
